From 23d07e488e482e492ae385c12c6c2c5f66e36a71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YOUR NAME <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:58:36 +0900
Subject: [RFC PATCH 2/2] Input: add driver for the Lenovo TB710FU Keyboard
 Pack

The Keyboard Pack is a detachable keyboard with a touchpad for the Lenovo
TB710FU tablet. It sends scrambled reports over a 921600 baud UART on the
pogo pins. Add a serdev driver that exposes the keyboard, the touchpad
and the fold state as input devices.

The pogo pins are powered only while a keyboard is attached, and the
input devices exist only during that time. Plug detection is a GPIO that
the board describes as a gpio-keys SW_DOCK switch, which the driver
follows with an input handler.

The protocol and the scrambling table were obtained by disassembling the
vendor kernel module (lenovo_keyboard.ko) and observing the UART traffic.

This driver was written with an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5)
working from the submitter's hardware testing, and reviewed by the
submitter.
